      "side": 0,
      "message": "Yes, that\u0027s intentional. It\u0027s actually the main piece of the fix. The group_filter has to be ignored here so that the only caller of this method (delete_user) can see all groups of which this user is a member and therefore can remove them from all of those groups, so we\u0027re not leaving behind member references for a deleted user. This also fits with the name of the method, as opposed to the list_user_groups_filtered method immediately after it, so I would not expect to see other code that wants filtering to start using this and be broken... they would use the filtered method..",
